# ArgoCD GitOps Lab – Kubernetes Deployment

## 1. Project Overview

This project demonstrates GitOps using **ArgoCD, Kubernetes, GitHub and Kustomize**.

ArgoCD continuously monitors the GitHub repository and automatically deploys Kubernetes resources whenever changes are pushed to the configured Git branch.

The application deployed in this lab is an NGINX web server running with two replicas inside a Minikube Kubernetes cluster.

## 2. Technologies Used

- Kubernetes
- Minikube
- ArgoCD Core
- Git and GitHub
- Kustomize
- NGINX
- Docker

## 3. Project Architecture

```text
GitHub Repository
       |
       | ArgoCD monitors Git
       v
ArgoCD Controller
       |
       | Synchronizes manifests
       v
Minikube Kubernetes Cluster
       |
       v
NGINX Deployment
       |
       +--- NGINX Pod 1
       |
       +--- NGINX Pod 2
       |
       v
NGINX ClusterIP Service
```

## 4. Project Structure

```text
ArgoCD-GitOps-Lab/
│
├── app/
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   └── kustomization.yaml
│
├── argocd/
│   ├── application.yaml
│   └── project.yaml
│
└── README.md
```

## 5. Kubernetes Configuration

### NGINX Deployment

- Deployment name: `gitops-nginx`
- Container image: `nginx:1.27-alpine`
- Replicas: 2
- Container port: 80
- CPU and memory requests and limits configured.

### Kubernetes Service

- Service name: `gitops-nginx`
- Service type: ClusterIP
- Service port: 80
- Target port: 80

### ArgoCD Application

- Application name: `argocd-gitops-lab`
- Namespace: `argocd`
- Git repository: `https://github.com/Anandhrosh/Devops-Intership-2026.git`
- Branch: `main`
- Manifest path: `ArgoCD-GitOps-Lab/app`

### Automated Sync Features

- Automated synchronization
- Self-healing enabled
- Automatic pruning enabled

## 6. Run the Existing Project

**Important:** The project has already been created and configured. You do not need to reinstall ArgoCD or recreate the Kubernetes resources every time.

### Step 1 – Start Minikube

Start the existing ArgoCD lab profile:

```bash
minikube start -p argocd-lab
```

### Step 2 – Set Kubernetes Context

```bash
kubectl config use-context argocd-lab
```

### Step 3 – Check Minikube

```bash
minikube status -p argocd-lab
```

Check the Kubernetes node:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

### Step 4 – Check ArgoCD

```bash
kubectl get pods -n argocd
```

Wait until the ArgoCD pods show `Running` and `1/1 Ready`.

### Step 5 – Check ArgoCD Application

```bash
kubectl get applications -n argocd
```

Expected result:

```text
NAME                SYNC STATUS   HEALTH STATUS
argocd-gitops-lab   Synced        Healthy
```

### Step 6 – Check NGINX Deployment

```bash
kubectl get deployments,pods,services -n default -l app=gitops-nginx
```

Expected:
- Deployment: 2/2 ready
- Pods: 2 Running
- Service: gitops-nginx

### Step 7 – Test NGINX Service

Run:

```bash
kubectl run nginx-test --rm -it --restart=Never --image=curlimages/curl -- curl -I http://gitops-nginx.default.svc.cluster.local
```

Expected response:

```text
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Server: nginx/1.27.5
```

Your application is running successfully!

## 7. How to Apply Future Changes (GitOps Workflow)

When you want to change the application:

**Step 1:** Edit the Kubernetes YAML files inside `app/`.

**Step 2:** Commit and push the changes to GitHub.

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "update nginx application"
git push origin main
```

**Step 3:** ArgoCD detects the GitHub changes and automatically synchronizes the Kubernetes cluster.

Check synchronization:

```bash
kubectl get application argocd-gitops-lab -n argocd
```

Check deployed resources:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n default -l app=gitops-nginx
```

## 8. Stop the Project

When you finish practicing, stop the Minikube profile:

```bash
minikube stop -p argocd-lab
```

This preserves the existing cluster configuration and resources.

To run the project again, follow Section 6.

## 9. Troubleshooting

### Check ArgoCD pods

```bash
kubectl get pods -n argocd
```

### Check Application details

```bash
kubectl describe application argocd-gitops-lab -n argocd
```

### Check Application Controller logs

```bash
kubectl logs statefulset/argocd-application-controller -n argocd
```

### Refresh Application status

```bash
kubectl annotate application argocd-gitops-lab -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite
```

### Check NGINX deployment

```bash
kubectl get deployment gitops-nginx -n default
```

